Z||000003||william_thorniii||02-02-2000||09:49 PM||||Eddie,<P>That is one magnificent vehicle.  My friends and I had always dreamed of finding a Z34 w/ a 5 spd.  We don't even care what running condition they are in because he wants one to drive and I just want to get my hands on the engine/tranny combo.  You really need to check out (http://mae.wvu.edu/~mhawkins/super34.htm) if you haven't already.  I have tried to get in touch with him without success.  Man those are rare, I just can't believe it.  Congratulations.  I would NOT put the ECM in the engine bay though.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-03-2000||03:56 AM||||I'm just curious now that I've really looked at those pics for a moment.  What size are the wheels?  16", right?  I wonder if they'd fit on a Fiero.  If they do and you don't want them, Eddie, LMK.  Maybe I could take them off your hands for a price.  Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||02-03-2000||11:36 AM||||Eddie, a couple years ago I went to a Fiero BBQ (we didn't BBQ a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) in Charleston, SC. We had about 20-some Fieros. One of those was a GT with a 3.4L from this car, I believe. The car was owned by Dwain Thier. I've got a listing of parts and prices he used for his conversion. According to his list, his engine develops 210hp@5200, 215#t@4000. His automatic engine was converted to a stick set up. Most everything is listed, flywheel, clutch, cables. He's a member of Space Coast Fieros, in FL. He calls his GT "Silver Thunder." I've got several pics of his car/engine. LMK if you'd like his contact info. I remember how sweet it sounded as it rumbled past us!! <BR>Take care  -joel ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eddie.H||02-03-2000||05:39 PM||||Monkeyman yes they are 16s. 225/16/60hr but they will note fit a fiero any way I have to let them go to the guy doing the work hes getting what ever is left after the swap thats how I am paying him . But the tires are 5000 miles new dunlop (d60 a2s) i have the same ones on my fiero but they are 14s I like dunlop tires you get a lot for your money||||reg||6
